## Delivered implementation and model-free proof

The existing T7 entry is the sole controller of one combined profile and private worker. The profile protects the entire original Root and all three existing immutable global-setting literals. All setup/MCP/Codex descendants inherit it; commandTask Codex processes no longer create a nested sandbox or leave the owned worker process group. A subordinate test-only helper validates canonical input/source/policy bindings and actual safe append-open denials plus an owned temporary write/read control before account/MCP/model access. Direct unguarded flags, wrong bindings, a weaker actual profile and failed positive controls stop. The controller reserves two slots exclusively before one real cohort, logs attempted/executed separately and applies a finite whole-window owned-tree deadline. Application/protection/account failures remain distinct. The bound Run launcher supplies inputs and retains results without another sandbox or permanent historical-file veto.

The original Core visibility/navigation implementation remains in its existing two owners, with no writer or authority expansion. The first new native session exposed insufficiently explicit pairing guidance. A same-scope correction now names target_source+primary_target in the normal-start description; target_source explicitly says Requires primary_target, and primary_target names target_source. The valid/rejected input sets and all semantic conditions are unchanged. This adds exactly one discovery/source byte. The correction was made only after both planned sessions and their protected comparison finished; no source changed between repetitions.

Fresh current-source checks passed:

- guard-integration-03: all four registered T7 test groups pass, zero real models; preserves original tuple/two-fixture/account-home/API-exclusion tests and adds actual OS inherited protection, direct flag/tamper/weaker-profile/positive-control/application failure and setup/worker/teardown deadline cases. Unrelated sentinel survives; owned descendants terminate. The initial guard-integration-01 test-Root overlap setup failure and later passing guard-integration-02 remain retained.
- pair-schema-01: all 247,003 SDK comparison cases and 160 frozen Core outcomes pass, zero acceptance differences; 24 retained old inputs replay equivalently and all 15 original SDK-invalid calls stay rejected.
- pair-cli-01 and pair-protocol-01: actual CLI/readiness/parity and SDK/STDIO navigation/historical/refusal cases pass, including both supported protocol versions.
- pair-renderer-01: installed Codex CLI 0.163.0 actually exposes all 14 input fields and 11 operations. Its retained signature includes both paired-property comments. One loopback stub request, no external network, account auth or model.
- pair-build-prepare-01, pair-compatibility-record-01 and pair-normal-build-01: canonical preparation/normal build pass. The diagnosed pair-compatibility-01 source_snapshot_changed is retained; reviewed canonical deterministic renewal evaluates 56 scenarios with zero unexpected failures, no native reruns or replacement historical inputs.
- pair-source-bindings-01 and pair-copilot-01: actual Root/candidate Core and assembled payload match. Inspect 4,993 <= 5,000 bytes; five command aggregate 23,254 and command/decision aggregate 24,509 <= 24,576; each command <= 8,192, input/output 65,536/1,048,576 unchanged. Copilot 397 files and 3,509,461 bytes equals its unchanged ceiling; no payload headroom remains.
